---
id: journey_system_cascade
title: Cascade Failure
tags: [danger, technical]
context: journey
weight: 10
cooldown: 6
---

=== intro

It starts with a flicker in your navigation subsystem. Then power fluctuations 
in the cargo hold. Then—

Warnings flood your consciousness. Multiple systems failing, each failure 
triggering another. A cascade, spreading through your infrastructure like 
disease through flesh.

You have seconds to decide.

* [Isolate and restart affected systems]
  -> isolate

* [Emergency shutdown—go dark]
  -> shutdown

* [Ride it out, trust your redundancies]
  -> ride

=== isolate

You partition your consciousness, cutting off the infected systems. It feels like 
losing fingers. The cascade slows, stops—but not before it claims your secondary 
navigation array.

The restart takes time. You drift in the dark, running on minimal power, 
rebuilding yourself piece by piece.

* [Complete the restart]
  ~ supplies -= 8
  ~ chronicle "System Cascade"
    Suffered a cascade failure. Lost secondary navigation, but contained the damage.
  -> END

=== shutdown

You go cold. Everything stops—thought, sensation, movement. For an eternal 
instant, you are nothing.

Then: restart. Systems coming online one by one, clean, uncorrupted. The cascade 
burned itself out against dead circuits.

But you've lost time. And fuel. Your reserves burned to keep core functions 
alive during the blackout.

* [Resume course]
  ~ fuel -= 12
  ~ damage integrity 5
  ~ chronicle "Emergency Shutdown"
    Initiated emergency shutdown during cascade failure. Lost time and fuel, but systems are clean.
  -> END

=== ride

You trust your design. The redundancies hold—barely. The cascade washes through 
your systems and ebbs, leaving damage in its wake.

You're still flying. That's something.

* [Assess the damage]
  ~ damage hull 10
  ~ supplies -= 5
  ~ chronicle "System Cascade"
    Rode out a cascade failure. Hull and systems took damage, but we're still operational.
  -> END
